1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:04,718
Most rooms at this Las Vegas Strip resort
come with a private terrace, and some of

2
00:00:04,748 --> 00:00:07,307
them look straight at the Bellagio
fountains.

3
00:00:07,437 --> 00:00:12,560
This is The Cosmopolitan of Las Vegas, a
five star resort rated eight point eight

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:16,504
out of ten on Expedia, from more than
eleven thousand reviews.

5
00:00:16,634 --> 00:00:22,340
It has nineteen restaurants, a bar built
inside a giant crystal chandelier, and a

6
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:24,039
spa with a Turkish bath.

7
00:00:24,169 --> 00:00:29,447
Here is the plan: the room to ask for, the
bar to see first, and my honest score at

8
00:00:29,477 --> 00:00:29,959
the end.

9
00:00:30,089 --> 00:00:31,659
Start with your room.

10
00:00:31,882 --> 00:00:36,991
There are about three thousand rooms in
two towers, and the ones you want are the

11
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:37,879
terrace rooms.

12
00:00:38,009 --> 00:00:42,668
A Terrace Studio is six hundred twenty
square feet, with a king bed and a private

13
00:00:42,698 --> 00:00:43,131
terrace.

14
00:00:43,261 --> 00:00:47,668
Ask for the fountain view, and you can
watch the Bellagio fountains from your own

15
00:00:47,698 --> 00:00:48,106
balcony.

16
00:00:48,236 --> 00:00:52,312
Guests score the Terrace Studio Fountain
View nine point zero out of ten.

17
00:00:52,442 --> 00:00:57,271
The Terrace One Bedroom Suite adds a
separate bedroom and a Japanese soaking
tub.

18
00:00:57,401 --> 00:00:59,356
Now, the heart of the resort.

19
00:00:59,486 --> 00:01:04,535
The Chandelier is a bar built inside a
giant crystal chandelier, right in the
middle

20
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:05,381
of the action.

21
00:01:05,511 --> 00:01:09,679
There are eight bars and lounges in all,
plus two poolside bars.

22
00:01:09,809 --> 00:01:14,170
CliQue is open from four in the afternoon
until three in the morning, every day.

23
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,777
And Ghost Donkey stays open until
midnight, and until four in the morning on
Fridays

24
00:01:18,807 --> 00:01:19,528
and Saturdays.

25
00:01:19,658 --> 00:01:20,728
Now, the food.

26
00:01:20,868 --> 00:01:25,563
There are nineteen restaurants and three
coffee shops, so you will never run out of

27
00:01:25,593 --> 00:01:26,018
choices.

28
00:01:26,148 --> 00:01:30,718
Dinner spots include Scarpetta, STK,
Jaleo, Momofuku, and Zuma.

29
00:01:31,983 --> 00:01:37,727
For breakfast, the Wicked Spoon Buffet and
The Henry are both open for breakfast,

30
00:01:37,757 --> 00:01:39,010
lunch, and dinner.

31
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:42,769
Want a late bite? Hattie B's Hot Chicken
is open until ten at night, and until

32
00:01:42,799 --> 00:01:44,364
midnight on Fridays and Saturdays.

33
00:01:44,494 --> 00:01:49,107
Guests say great things about the pool,
the central location, and the helpful
staff.

34
00:01:49,237 --> 00:01:50,236
Next, unwind.

35
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:56,015
The seasonal pool has cabanas, sun
loungers, and umbrellas, and Expedia lists
it as

36
00:01:56,045 --> 00:02:00,651
open from March to November, from ten in
the morning to four in the afternoon.

37
00:02:00,781 --> 00:02:06,572
Sahra Spa Salon and Hammam has couples
treatment rooms, a sauna, a hot tub, and a

38
00:02:06,602 --> 00:02:07,506
Turkish bath.

39
00:02:07,636 --> 00:02:11,377
The spa is open every day, with treatments
from nine in the morning to seven at

40
00:02:11,407 --> 00:02:11,663
night.

41
00:02:11,793 --> 00:02:13,828
You are right in the middle of the Strip.

42
00:02:13,958 --> 00:02:18,762
The Bellagio fountains are a three minute
walk, and Crystals at City Center is two.

43
00:02:18,892 --> 00:02:22,713
The airport is a short drive away, and
Expedia says you do not need a car.

44
00:02:22,843 --> 00:02:24,861
A few tips to enjoy it even more.

45
00:02:24,991 --> 00:02:28,966
Book a terrace room, because the terrace
is what makes this place special, and ask

46
00:02:28,996 --> 00:02:30,040
for the fountain view.

47
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:34,468
There is a daily resort fee, and it
includes fitness center access, internet,
and

48
00:02:34,498 --> 00:02:35,109
phone calls.

49
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:39,722
Parking is not free: covered self parking
is twenty dollars a day, and valet is

50
00:02:39,752 --> 00:02:40,065
forty.

51
00:02:40,195 --> 00:02:44,481
Check in starts at three in the afternoon,
check out is by eleven, and the minimum

52
00:02:44,511 --> 00:02:45,429
age is twenty one.

53
00:02:45,559 --> 00:02:47,949
So, is The Cosmopolitan worth it?

54
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:52,640
On Expedia, guests give it eight point
eight out of ten, and about seven in ten

55
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:54,500
reviewers gave it a perfect ten.

56
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:59,094
Cleanliness scores nine point zero,
amenities nine point zero, and staff and
service

57
00:02:59,124 --> 00:03:00,057
eight point eight.

58
00:03:00,187 --> 00:03:02,425
My honest score is nine out of ten.

59
00:03:02,555 --> 00:03:06,629
It is a great pick for couples and friends
who want a terrace, great food, and a

60
00:03:06,659 --> 00:03:08,630
lively stay in the middle of the Strip.

61
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,044
The link is in the description.
